                <pb facs="0293" n="181" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg181"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">762.94/58: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dodd</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-25T13:00:00+01:00">May 25, 1935—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 25—9:22 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>111. An usually very dependable source claims that a secret German-Japanese
                    military alliance has just been concluded and that 70 Japanese officers are
                    coming to Germany for liaison purposes.</p>
                <p>It will take some time to reach conclusions as to truth of this statement here,
                    so submit it with all reserve.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodd</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
